This directory bundles plink.exe and pscp.exe from the PuTTY project
(https://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/putty/), used here for
unattended SSH password authentication - Windows' own built-in OpenSSH
client cannot read a password from a non-interactive stdin at all, so
there is no dependency-free way to script password-based SSH from
PowerShell without a different tool.

Install-ClientDebianSSH.ps1 writes the password to a short-lived,
current-user-only temp file and passes it via plink's/pscp's -pwfile
argument (added in PuTTY 0.81) rather than the -pw command-line argument,
so the password never appears in a local process listing (Get-CimInstance
Win32_Process, Task Manager) for the duration of the connection. The temp
file's contents are overwritten before deletion once the connection
completes.

